WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.001 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Welcome to the show!

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:03.203 size:84% position:42%
-I'm wearing a suit.
-You're wearing a suit.

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:04.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
You look very dapper.
-Thank you.

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:05.872 line:92%
-But I want to ask about this

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:08.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you did a very
non-suit activity recently.

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:11.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
You went to a survival --
what is it called?

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:15.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
A survival training camp?
-Yes. We did not wear suits.

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:17.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I would imagine.
-You're right,

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was a wilderness
survival retreat.

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:22.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, a weekend? Two days?
A day?

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:24.924
-It was a three-day course
where me and my friends learned

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:28.595
how to survive in the wilderness
without the things

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:30.163 line:92%
that you normally have on hand.

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:33.633
-What brought this about as
something you wanted to do?

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:34.968 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Um...

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:37.370 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.139 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Living in California,

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:42.542
I realized I live very near
where a lot of earthquakes --

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:44.044 line:92%
there could be a big earthquake,

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:46.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
things could fall down,
lots of things.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:50.150
[Sighs] I guess I was dipping
my toes into doomsday prepping.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.
-A little bit, if you will.

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:54.687
-Just a little toe dip.
And after the three days,

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:57.757 size:88% position:44%
do you feel better about
your family's chances?

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:58.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-Okay.

00:00:58.892 --> 00:00:59.826 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:04.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm now actually wilderness
first-aid certified.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:05.765 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Oh that's pretty good.

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's true. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:09.202 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:10.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now a lot of people
don't know this,

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.272 size:75% position:38%
but to be wilderness
first-aid certified,

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.307
you're not actually really
supposed to treat the person.

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:16.276 size:78% position:39%
You're just supposed
to keep them alive...

00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:17.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-...until somebody

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
who actually knows something
shows up.

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:20.246 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:22.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
So a lot of it's really
just like, "Hey, I'm here.

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:25.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm here. I'm here for you."
You know what I mean?

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:26.820 size:78% position:39%
-Like "Stay with me,"
that kind of thing?

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, yeah, yeah, yeah,
"Stay with me."

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:30.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
And slapping them.
-Oh, gotcha.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:32.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-"Don't you leave me!"

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:33.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, "Don't you die on me,
you son of a bitch."

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.161 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah, don't you die --
Oh, that's a good one.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.629
You son of a bitch. Right.
-Yeah, that kind of thing

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:39.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
until the chopper shows up,
and then you're, like,

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:40.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm out of here.
-Wow.

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:42.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But yeah, no --
I guess I just felt like

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:46.372
I wanted to make sure that
I knew how to do basic things

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:47.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
that --
-Yes.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We got so comfortable
in society.

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:49.876 line:92%
You know, we have running water,

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:51.811
and I didn't realize, you know,
ask a lot of people,

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.646
like, what's the first thing
that will kill you if you're

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
lost in the wilderness,
and you're injured,

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
and most people say. well,
well you'll --

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:58.351 size:88% position:44% line:92%
you'll run out of water.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
You'll be very, very thirsty,
and you'll die of --

00:02:00.854 --> 00:02:03.656
whatever that's called, when you
die of not having enough water.

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:06.493 line:92%
And it's actually exposure.

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:08.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just to --
-To the elements.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:08.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
-To the elements.
-Yeah.

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:09.829 line:92%
So, if you sleep on the ground,

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:11.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know,
it's warm outside,

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:12.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
if it gets cold at night,
you'll die

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:14.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
because the ground
will freeze you to death.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:18.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you've got to build like
a thing,

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:19.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
and put leaves in there.
-Wow!

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:21.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know what I mean?
And so, but you'll die later

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:23.276
of Lyme disease, because there's
ticks in the leaves.

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:23.810 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But you'll buy yourself
a couple of days.

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.213
-You'll buy yourself a couple --
and then a life of misery

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:30.150
suffering from Lyme disease.
But yeah, in the meantime --

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:31.951
-You -- I think you and I
are very similar 'cause --

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:35.588
well first, congratulations,
"Always Sunny," 12 seasons,

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:38.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is -- like,
no one does that.

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:39.659 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:44.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've also been working in TV
for a while now,

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:46.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
and do you think that you
now officially --

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.168 size:88% position:44%
because I feel this way.
I officially don't know

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:51.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
how to do anything of value --
like of real-life value.

00:02:51.538 --> 00:02:53.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, I see. Yeah,
you get comfortable, right?

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:56.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah, I think that's true.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:57.010 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Were you ever handy?

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:01.214
Were you ever somebody who could
fix something in your house?

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:03.483 line:92%
-My -- yeah. Yes, absolutely.

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:05.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, like I had to
cut the grass.

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:06.586 line:92%
I had to trim the hedges,

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:08.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I had to fix stuff
around the --

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:10.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
But my dad didn't teach me
a ton of stuff.

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:11.791
You know, even though he kind
of knew how to do that stuff,

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:15.195
I think he wanted to like, I
don't know, shelter us from it

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:15.962 line:92%
and not make us have to do that.

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:17.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had to learn --
when I was in theatre school,

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.866
I had to learn stagecraft, so
I learned how to use some tools,

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:22.302
and I would fix things in
the house when they got broken.

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:24.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, but, yeah, you do.
You get comfortable,

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:26.906
and after while you realize,
like, I don't want to do that,

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:28.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm going to hire somebody
to do it.

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:29.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
The most depressing thing

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:34.547
in my life is my wife's dad is,
like, a builder,

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:37.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
and her brother
knows everything,

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:38.551 size:78% position:39%
and so when something
breaks in our house,

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's really emasculating
because one of them shows up

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:43.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
with a tool belt, and is like,
"Hey, what are you doing?"

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:45.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "Let me put down
this Xbox controller

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:49.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
and pretend to see
what you're seeing."

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:52.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I can tell you
how to fix chapped lips.

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:54.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah?
-But --

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.302 line:92%
-Everybody says that about you!

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:57.036 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.036 --> 00:04:01.274
-But I can't teach you how to
fix, you know, a light switch.

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:03.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-No, it's sad.

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:05.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
You sort of forget to --
I mean, you can --

00:04:05.245 --> 00:04:07.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think to a certain degree,
we all suffer from this.

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:09.315 size:88% position:44%
But if you start to make
a little bit of dough,

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:11.484
you start to realize, I'm going
to pay a guy to do that.

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:12.318 line:92%
I'll pay a guy to do this,

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:14.087
and I'm worried that I'm
not going to teach my kids,

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:16.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I have two boys.
-Yeah.

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:16.990 line:92%
-You know, and like I said,

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
I used to cut the grass
and all that.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:19.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, I don't want them
cutting my grass,

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:21.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I don't want them
messing up my grass.

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:22.996 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.996 --> 00:04:26.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know? Whereas like,
my dad was like,

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:27.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You're cutting the grass."
-Yeah.

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:30.370
-And I'm like, mnh.
-I also just worry about how --

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:33.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
my dad knows a lot
about everything.

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:35.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, same.
-And now I just feel like,

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:37.543 size:88% position:44%
because of the Internet,
anything my kid asks me,

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:39.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll be like,
"Let's go over to the laptop."

00:04:39.579 --> 00:04:40.113 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:41.981
-Yeah, the box of knowledge.
-That's a good question, yeah.

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:43.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Let's go to the box
of knowledge.

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:44.617 size:75% position:38%
-This is where daddy
put all his ideas.

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:46.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, and take credit for it.

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:47.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and now we can
go find them.

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:49.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I built this box of knowledge
for you, son,

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:53.159
so that when I pass on --
it's like Superman and his dad,

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:56.029
he was like the crystal thing --
-Right.

